# Release binaries belong in GitHub Releases (CDN-served), NEVER in
# git history.  A 145 MB .dmg committed once stays in the repo forever
# and balloons every fresh clone.
#
# If you ever need to publish-then-commit metadata about a binary
# (size, sha256, etc.), do it in CHANGELOG.md or docs/ — never the
# binary itself.

# macOS installer images
*.dmg
*.pkg

# Tauri auto-updater payloads
*.app.tar.gz
*.app.tar.gz.sig

# Tauri updater manifest (we mint one per release as an asset)
latest.json

# Generic build/archive bycatch
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz

# macOS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editor configs that shouldn't escape this machine
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
